SWEET synthetic swipe cadence in milliseconds (patch 0220, boot-arg sweetswipems=N, default off; T-359f, G-F55): replaces the whole-second gap between the finger-up of one synthetic swipe (0152) and the finger-down of the next with N ms (N 1..60000; a larger value is ignored with a SWEET GAP line), so a swipe can start while the previous animation still runs. sweetswipe=N must still be set (it enables the swipes, the 120 s start delay and the count of 0155). Logs 'SWEET HID: synthetic swipes every N ms'. Applies on top of 0152/0155. No hardware access, no register or store.
